      "reasons": [
        "The packet describes supported housing facilities as an “ideal setting” for supporting people with severe mental illness, and that the most successfully implemented interventions were “multidisciplinary and integrated into standard care,” but it does not explicitly define supported housing as a housing environment where “support is available as part of their living environment.”",
        "The definition’s phrase “health-related support and other care can be integrated into standard services” is only partially supported; the packet supports integration into “standard care” in the context of interventions, not the broader claim about “health-related support and other care” being integrated into “standard services.”"
      ],
